{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1109802-character-seeds","id":1109802,"title":"Character seeds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-30T09:48:52-07:00","id":1109802,"title":"Character seeds","content":"I'm starting a game where half the players have never roleplayed, and one has only done DnD type games. To help them, I put together short character seeds to get their imaginations going. I thought a thread with prompts like this might be useful for PCs or NPCs.<br /> <br /> *******<br /> <br /> &quot;You'll be back,&quot; they said, when you went south to find a better life in thriving Andhaven. But the hills tug at your heart and the locals touch their wallets when they pass you. Do you have what it takes to make a life in the city?<br /> <br /> A clever paparazzi can get the money shots without breaking the letter of the law. In Sarnia, the spirit is a little less forgiving. You've got to be clever, and lucky, or risk a trumped up charge or an accident from a zealous bodyguard.<br /> <br /> Aldrenna, St. Catherine, then the estates and bungalows in between... there's a lot of wealth to be had. But unlike the Riviera, the resorts here are smaller, more intimate. Faces are more noticeable. Looks like someone noticed you. Do you go to ground, or risk fencing the loot first?<br /> <br /> You knew going into police work that big cities come with big city problems. But when a group of men suggest that it would be in your best interest to ignore certain activities in exchange for a piece of the action, that's a choice you hadn't expected.<br /> <br /> Two weeks in Sarnia. Why? Well, initially, because the package deal made it the cheapest place that reliably speaks English outside of North America. You can tell your friends you vacationed in Europe. You don't have to tell them you emptied your accounts to do it. But, hell, it's another country! So... what is there to do here, anyway?<br /> <br /> At 18, you had a purpose. At 35, you have a scar, a couple of medals, a pension, and some really bad memories. For a month now, you've had no one to tell you what to do. It's time to pick a direction...or just self-medicate until other choices vanish.<br /> <br /> &quot;Just look at this map. See how these five castles align with this series of dolmens, and how they circle Mont Belmuno? Now, look at the infrared photo of the island. You see it, don't you? Those castles weren't just there to protect soldiers, they were there to protect the energy nexi that center around the hill.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I wouldn't know nuffin 'bout that. Hm? Davvies told you I did? Where'd you see 'im? Well, alright. I know a fella who knows a guy, you follow? Tell you what. Show me you're serious, and I'll see what I can find out.&quot;<br /> <br /> Your work doesn't usually take you across the Channel; some computer searches, legwork and a telephoto lens get you the evidence you need to satisfy your clients. But this one is paying for you to follow her trail, and the trail leads to Sarnia.<br /> <br /> You planned it perfectly, over the course of months. Now it's time. He thinks you're going to Croydon to visit a friend, but by tomorrow night you'll be in Sarnia... where his-- <i>your</i> -- little nest egg is waiting.<br /> <br /> You climbed out of your crib and though the pet flap. All your life, you've been going where you don't belong. You're an Urban Explorer, and you just know that Sarnia has bunkers and tunnels that haven't been seen since '45.<br /> <br /> The last note from Stewart said the cell was compromised. The armory was gone. He said to get out like you planned, use the fake papers, and if anyone was left they would contact you in a month. With luck, the security services wouldn't get wind of you in Sarnia.<br /> <br /> The last note from Stewart said the cell was compromised. The armory was gone. He said to get out like you planned, use the fake papers, and if anyone was left they would contact you in a month. With luck, the vampires wouldn't get wind of you in Sarnia.<br /> <br /> This is a nice bench. Good. It's not raining. That's a start. Let's work from there. Ah, trouser pockets. Wallet? No. Damn. Is that woman staring at me? Maybe she knows my name. Maybe she'll tell me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}